        prompts: {
          human: 'Three-player Tarot from 1637: declare combinations for marques, follow suit, play trumps when unable to follow, excuse the Fool before the last trick; Ultimo and card points determine payments.',
          ai: 'Game: Tarot of the Abbé de Marolles 1637. Three players, 66 cards. Declarations then tricks; follow suit, must play trump if cannot follow; Fool excuses; Tarots and Ultimo pay marques; card points above/below 25 settle winner/losers.',
        },
        scoring: {
          description: 'Marques are won or paid for: declarations (Tarots, Kings+Fool, Triomphes, Imperials, Brizigole, Tous les trois), playing or capturing Tarots in tricks, Ultimo (last trick with King or Trump I), and card points (Tarots 5, Queens 4, Cavaliers 3, Jacks 2; pack total 74). Below 25 points = loser pays winner(s); above 25 = winner collects.',
          winCondition: 'After the hand, the player(s) with above-average card points (25 or more) win; the player(s) with below average (24 or less) pay. Two losers each pay the single winner per 5-point band below 25; two winners each collect from the single loser per 5-point band above 25. Ultimo (last trick with King or Trump I) pays 6 marques from each opponent.',
